<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37483" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξοικ-ειόω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>appropriate, assimilate,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μένε μέχρι -ειώσῃς σεαυτῷ καὶ ταῦτα,
					ὡς ὁ ἐρρωμένος στόμαχος πάντα -ειοῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					M.Ant.
					10.31
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.46
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			):—
				Med.
			, <i>appropriate,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χώραν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					4.1.8
				</span></i>
			; <i>conciliate, win over,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				5.4.12
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνθρώπους μεταδόσει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					2.3.4
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>BJ</u>
				1.8.9
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄχλον εἴς τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.529
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξοικειοῦσθαί τινι</span>
			<i>adapt oneself to</i> one, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.649e
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>reduce to its proper nature,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.298
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
